      "op": "spawn",
      "role": "builder",
      "task": "Write module.py exposing solve(data) per the user contract, and test_cases.json. Contract: data={'ops': [...]}; each op has 'kind' and maybe 'amount'/'id'. Apply in order; return {'balance':int,'held':int,'available':int} (available=balance-held). Checks in exact order per op: (1) kind must be credit/debit/hold/release else ValueError. (2) for credit/debit/hold, amount must be int >=1; bool is rejected -> ValueError. (3) hold: id must not already be an active hold; release: id must be an active hold; else ValueError. (4) debit/hold: amount must not exceed available (balance - held) else ValueError. credit adds to balance; debit subtracts; hold adds active hold id->amount; release removes hold, ignoring any amount. First failing op raises; empty ops returns zeros. Do not mutate input. Python stdlib only, no I/O. test_cases.json: JSON list of at least 6 distinct cases, each {name, input, output} or {name, input, error:'ValueError'}; cover empty, credit/debit, hold/release, release ignoring amount, bool amount, unknown kind, duplicate hold id, release unknown id, debit exceeding available after hold, amount 0, check ordering (e.g. invalid kind before amount). Expectations must match the contract exactly."
    },
